    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nSince 3.3.0, annotating a module level global with `typing.Final` crashes the compiler when the same name is also declared in the module's `.pxd`. \n\nThe crash is in the new code that checks global annotations against the `.pxd` declaration (added for #7877). `analyse_as_type()` returns `None` for `Final[...]` because Cython does not know `typing.Final`, and the result is used without a `None` check:\n\n```\nfinalmod.py:3:0: Compiler crash in AnalyseDeclarationsTransform\n...\nFile 'ExprNodes.py', line 2377, in _analyse_target_declaration: NameNode(finalmod.py:3:0,\n    name = 'LIMIT',\n    ...)\n\nCompiler crash traceback from this point on:\n  File \".../Cython/Compiler/ExprNodes.py\", line 2377, in _analyse_target_declaration\n    if not (annotation_type.assignable_from(entry_type) or entry_type.assignable_from(annotation_type)):\n            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nAttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'assignable_from'\n```\n\nBare `Final` and a string annotation `\"Final[int]\"` crash the same way. \n\nThe same annotation on a global that is not in the `.pxd` compiles fine, and the same file compiles fine with 3.2.x, where global annotations were ignored.\n\n\n\n### Code to reproduce the behaviour:\n\n\n`finalmod.py`\n\n```cython\nfrom typing import Final\n\nLIMIT: Final[int] = 128\n\n\ndef bump(x: int) -> int:\n    return x + LIMIT\n```\n\n`finalmod.pxd`\n\n```cython\ncdef unsigned int LIMIT\n```\n\n```\ncython -3 finalmod.py\n```\n\n\n\n### Expected behaviour\n\nThe file compiles, as it does with 3.2.x. `Final` is only a hint for static type checkers and should not affect the generated code. \n\n### OS\n\nmacOS 15\n\n### Python version\n\n3.14.2\n\n### Cython version\n\n3.3.0\n\n### Additional context\n\nFound while bumping Cython in `aiohttp`, which compiles a pure Python websocket reader with a `.pxd` for the C typing. \n\nWe had to drop `Final` from several module constants to get 3.3.0 to compile the module (aio-libs/aiohttp#13521, aio-libs/aiohttp#13547). ",
